{:edb/db-before-t 1240 :edb/db-after-t 1241 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534553 50 #inst "2026-10-12T02:52:00.835Z" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186124318 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ![](images/62/62cc7238e6676b8a43d216ab6c8b30504602c68fd548832eceac9b710b885471.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\n- If ![](images/b8/b85d717afa8af39d10517f909a09b53e6d379beef6e04e3d9ce7d3e48c88dca4.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\n- If ![](images/8e/8e12a5386c3db2149324bd28c174a5410f7751e0c963cf80969e0cfdf14e5d7b.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 false] [17592186124318 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If ![](images/77/77c0dd8d9b925b3310c5470f272b59e2b9d25bb141295741f1748771b6c454c1.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\nII. If ![](images/86/86c4f440750b5d7bf45e8c36b6fd9852c2749ac56331b3e0d76a6901acaf5b60.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\nIII. If ![](images/22/2295be7f70c3de36b51784b2919af95695f5520abdb2300287a17852b4cbfce3.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186124319 1071 "Given ![](images/82/829e66e040815801f77e92b2afd97531779864935faf7c9dcf1b0485593db856.svg) what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186124319 1071 "Given ![](images/e2/e20df1b44d2bfe100499eebfb4d2bdf8c1055978fdccbe11c8b5c0882052ace8.png) what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 false] [17592186124508 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425405 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186124508 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425406 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186124509 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425407 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186124510 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425404 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186124684 1050 420.0 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186125778 1064 "We already learned that the rank of a matrix $A$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ Now, can we obtain any information from the *non-pivot* columns?\n\nThe answer is yes! The non-pivot columns help to find the dimension of the null space of a matrix $A,$ and here's how.\n\nConsider the matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A$ is already in row echelon form, where the $1$st and the $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd one is a *non-pivot* column. Now, to get the null space of $A,$ we need to find the solution of the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\color{blue}x_1$ and ${\\color{blue}x_3}$ are basic variables and $\\color{red}x_2$ is a free variable. Hence, we obtain that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))={\\color{red}1}$.\n\nIn other words,\n\n> $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is equal to the number of *non-pivot* columns in the corresponding row echelon form of $A$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n> $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$  is the number of *free variables* in the corresponding homogeneous system with the coefficient matrix $A.$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 false] [17592186125778 1064 "We already learned that the rank of a matrix $A$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ Now, can we obtain any information from the *non-pivot* columns?\n\nThe answer is yes! The non-pivot columns help to find the dimension of the null space of a matrix $A,$ and here's how.\n\nConsider the matrix \n![](images/99/991b6f0c69e6341620139db9bfce5303785be21760eb8d630bfee92c57d4bc6a.svg)\n\nThe matrix $A$ is already in row echelon form, where the $1$st and the $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd one is a *non-pivot* column. Now, to get the null space of $A,$ we need to find the solution of the system\n\n![](images/1c/1cd56dc26ad4f478c3d7cb14375b8b2e45ef68e3215e79494d56108fecec39cb.svg)\n\nwhere $\\color{blue}x_1$ and ${\\color{blue}x_3}$ are basic variables and $\\color{red}x_2$ is a free variable. Hence, we obtain that \n\n![](images/56/56587dc5c1c98493060edb3561c13aa1576187461418619684459dd1f55626fe.svg)\n\nis a basis of $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))={\\color{red}1}$.\n\nIn other words,\n\n$\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is equal to the number of *non-pivot* columns in the corresponding row echelon form of $A$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$  is the number of *free variables* in the corresponding homogeneous system with the coefficient matrix $A.$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186319352 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 false] [17592186319352 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n\nII. If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n\nIII. If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425380 1080 "1" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425380 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425380 1083 #uuid "01b39024-8f98-5edf-93f7-04a64ee7b6c0" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425381 1080 "6" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425381 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534553 17592186045417 true]