 17592186425382 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425402 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425387 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425402 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425391 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425402 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425393 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425402 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425394 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425402 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425402 1077 "selection" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425402 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425382 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425402 1079 #uuid "f7861d69-8891-56f9-b3bb-6cd69873e91d" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425383 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425385 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425389 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425395 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425398 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1077 "selection" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425383 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425403 1079 #uuid "f829e1c6-fc4a-5157-b1d9-91868b24b67e" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425404 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425400 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425404 1069 "q-35347" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425404 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425404 1071 "Given $G=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))?$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425404 1072 #uuid "83850766-9b1b-5a37-bf38-12d47d12c4d5" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425404 1074 "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))$, we reduce $G$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{11}{4} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))=0.\n$$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425405 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425403 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425405 1069 "q-79338" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425405 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425405 1071 "If $B$ is a $4\\times 6$ matrix that has $4$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425405 1072 #uuid "85da25d6-54a2-55b2-b4ae-23095c708e42" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425405 1074 "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(B))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $B.$\n\nSince we are told that $B$ has $4$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=4.\n$$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425406 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425401 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425406 1069 "q-34901" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425406 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425406 1071 "If $A$ is a $7\\times 11$ matrix that has $7$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425406 1072 #uuid "b000b980-8b9a-5a4e-a59b-6de7017a3b28" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425406 1074 "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A.$\n\nSince we are told that $A$ has $7$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=7.\n$$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425407 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425402 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425407 1069 "q-35200" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425407 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425407 1071 "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425407 1072 #uuid "fd86946f-a577-5d18-8f57-7b7435272376" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true] [17592186425407 1074 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+2=3.\n$$" 13194139534553 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-01b39024-8f98-5edf-93f7-04a64ee7b6c0" 17592186425380 "answer-1b7137d1-196e-5467-891f-8a544f21aeba" 17592186425381 "answer-25d9c3ae-c6